findings.body:
The last commit deleted `@MainActor` from the class:

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Library/Bookmarks/EditBookmarkViewModelTests.swift" lines="9-12"}

`EditBookmarkViewModel.selectFolder(_:)` and `createNewFolder()` are explicitly `@MainActor`, and `onFolderStatusUpdate` is a `@MainActor` callback. Without class-level isolation, the sync test methods now call `subject.selectFolder(...)` (lines 60, 76, 78, 101, 113, 173) from a synchronous nonisolated context. That is a warning under Swift 5 strict checking and an error in Swift 6 mode, which defeats the point of a "fix warnings for Swift 6" PR.

It also means the new `async` `setUp`/`tearDown` run off the main thread, unlike the sync versions they replace.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Library/Bookmarks/EditBookmarkViewModelTests.swift" lines="11-11"}
@MainActor
class EditBookmarkViewModelTests: XCTestCase {

An earlier commit in this branch ("Fix teardown methods orders") put `try await super.tearDown()` last. The final commit moves it back to first in two suites:

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Frontend/StoriesFeed/StoriesFeedDiffableDataSourceTests.swift" lines="28-33"}

The same happens in ::file{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Helpers/RatingPromptManagerTests.swift"} (lines 36-46). The convention is set-up base-first and tear-down subclass-first. The rest of this PR follows it: it fixes HistoryPanelTests, IntroViewControllerTests and IntroViewModelTests to call super last. These two suites are now the inconsistent ones, and any state XCTestCase tears down (e.g. `addTeardownBlock` handlers) runs before `DependencyHelperMock().reset()` and `prefs.clearAll()`.

